# Ended-observation counter-example. A well-formed Observation (one vantage, one observed
# feature) whose validity interval has ended and that carries no gmeow:displayable value. An
# ended validity interval is not a reason to hide a record, so validation must conform and
# draw no display-suppression warning.

@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/shapes/> .
@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix xsd:   <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

ex:endedObservation a gmeow:Observation ;
    gmeow:vantage ex:endedObserver ;
    gmeow:observedFeature ex:endedFeature ;
    gmeow:validFrom  "2018-01-01T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    gmeow:validUntil "2019-01-01T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

ex:endedObserver a gmeow:Standpoint .
ex:endedFeature a gmeow:Place .
